  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404490",
      "title": "Sending POST Http Requests",
      "lectureOrder": 163,
      "videoOrder": 159,
      "sourceHash": "be9705769986f5d73605960607e97861bbe690ef0677c11f2942ecfeb2706a7c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 4.06,
          "en": "So how should we get started?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.06,
          "end": 7.24,
          "en": "What is the first kind of request we wanna send?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.24,
          "end": 10.44,
          "en": "Well, I would argue that it makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.44,
          "end": 15.31,
          "en": "that we start with adding expenses besides storing them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.31,
          "end": 19.27,
          "en": "in our local context, which we as mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.27,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "still might want to do so that we still have an offline copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 25.16,
          "en": "which we can view, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.16,
          "end": 27.25,
          "en": "without having an internet connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.25,
          "end": 28.6,
          "en": "So despite doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.6,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "we also wanna send it to this fire base back and API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 35.31,
          "en": "which we set up and to do all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.31,
          "end": 38.03,
          "en": "I will create a number utility helper file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.03,
          "end": 41.2,
          "en": "which I will name http.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.2,
          "end": 44.13,
          "en": "And it is in that file where I will want to create a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.13,
          "end": 48.85,
          "en": "of helper functions that help with sending requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.85,
          "end": 51.26,
          "en": "For example, here in http.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.26,
          "end": 53.56,
          "en": "we could create a function called storeexpense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.31,
          "end": 60.12,
          "en": "and we could expect to get our expense data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.12,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "And then here, the goal is to create such a http request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "and send it to fire base.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 69.91,
          "en": "Now this can be done with this axios package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.91,
          "end": 73.38,
          "en": "so we can import axios from axios.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.38,
          "end": 76.1,
          "en": "So use this third party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.1,
          "end": 79.4,
          "en": "and axios makes sending requests super simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.4,
          "end": 81.92,
          "en": "We can't just call a couple of helper methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.92,
          "end": 84.44,
          "en": "on this axios object, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.44,
          "end": 87.32,
          "en": "post to send a post request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.32,
          "end": 89.58,
          "en": "And we want to send a post request here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.58,
          "end": 91.64,
          "en": "for adding a new expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.64,
          "end": 94.64,
          "en": "So for saving a new piece of data on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.64,
          "end": 97.74000000000001,
          "en": "because the fire base API here wants us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.74000000000001,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "to send a post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 102.47,
          "en": "if we wanna create a new piece of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.47,
          "end": 104.5,
          "en": "You can check the official docs of fire base",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.5,
          "end": 108.14,
          "en": "to learn which request is expected for which kind of action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.14,
          "end": 111.86,
          "en": "but it is a post request for creating new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.86,
          "end": 114.74000000000001,
          "en": "So the post method of axios helps us send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.74000000000001,
          "end": 117.46000000000001,
          "en": "such a request, and now we need to pass the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.61,
          "end": 121.01,
          "en": "to which the request should be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.01,
          "end": 124.293,
          "en": "as a string, as a first argument to post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 127.69,
          "en": "And the URL is this URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.69,
          "end": 130.71,
          "en": "You can copy this URL here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.6,
          "end": 135.08,
          "en": "and paste it here, or to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.08,
          "end": 137.81,
          "en": "That's only a part of the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.81,
          "end": 140.63,
          "en": "Actually, this is the, the root URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.63,
          "end": 142.93,
          "en": "Now we can add more segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.93,
          "end": 146.55,
          "en": "after this root, for example, expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.55,
          "end": 149.51,
          "en": "And we have to add .json here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.51,
          "end": 153.07999999999998,
          "en": "Now this .json part is fire base specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.07999999999998,
          "end": 154.03,
          "en": "has nothing to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.03,
          "end": 157.61,
          "en": "with react native or react or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.61,
          "end": 160.602,
          "en": "Fire base just wants this .json at the end here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.602,
          "end": 164.7,
          "en": "to understand that we're targeting a specific node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.7,
          "end": 167.09,
          "en": "in the database. So to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.09,
          "end": 170.335,
          "en": "Now you can add any segments you want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.335,
          "end": 173.03,
          "en": "And those segments will be translated as nodes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.03,
          "end": 177.32,
          "en": "or to folders you could say in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.32,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "So this will create an expenses node in this database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 182.895,
          "en": "which we will see soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.895,
          "end": 184.82,
          "en": "Once we added our first expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.82,
          "end": 187.04,
          "en": "and under that expenses node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.04,
          "end": 189.903,
          "en": "we will find the newly added expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.75,
          "end": 194.23,
          "en": "So that's the URL to which we wanna send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.23,
          "end": 197.48,
          "en": "Now, as a second argument to the post method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.48,
          "end": 201.11,
          "en": "we have to define the value that should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.11,
          "end": 203.81,
          "en": "And in my case here that is this expense data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.81,
          "end": 205.82,
          "en": "which I expect to be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.82,
          "end": 209.14,
          "en": "that holds the amount, description and date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.14,
          "end": 211.695,
          "en": "not the ID, because an ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.695,
          "end": 216,
          "en": "a unique ID will be auto-generated by Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 217.41,
          "en": "which is pretty convenient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.41,
          "end": 220.152,
          "en": "because that allows us to get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.152,
          "end": 223.35,
          "en": "of our custom pseudo unique ID generation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.35,
          "end": 225.73,
          "en": "which we have here in the context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.73,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "But that will be one of the later steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 230.84,
          "en": "So that will send such a post request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.84,
          "end": 234.59300000000002,
          "en": "And for a start that is all we have to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.59300000000002,
          "end": 237.09,
          "en": "that will send such a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.09,
          "end": 240.56,
          "en": "So now we can actually export this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.56,
          "end": 245.35,
          "en": "to make it available outside of this utility http file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.35,
          "end": 250.06,
          "en": "and in manage expense, we can use it to send a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 250.06,
          "end": 253.32,
          "en": "Here, in confirm handler if we are not editing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 253.32,
          "end": 258.32,
          "en": "but adding we can use this store expense function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.55,
          "end": 259.573,
          "en": "and execute it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.89,
          "end": 265.89,
          "en": "Of course you must in import store expense from util/http.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.63,
          "end": 268.97,
          "en": "I can always get rid of some imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.97,
          "end": 271.12,
          "en": "that I don't need here anymore, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.09000000000003,
          "end": 274.83,
          "en": "But with store expense, imported like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.83,
          "end": 277.21,
          "en": "inside of the managed expense file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 277.21,
          "end": 281.99,
          "en": "we can call it to send this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.99,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "Now we need to provide our expense data to store expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 288.75,
          "en": "because that is expected as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.75,
          "end": 290.4,
          "en": "So therefore in managed expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 290.4,
          "end": 292.3,
          "en": "I do forward my expense data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.3,
          "end": 295.853,
          "en": "which is an object with description, amount and date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 296.8,
          "end": 299.4,
          "en": "Now we will improve this later, but for a start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.333,
          "end": 302.14,
          "en": "that is all we have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 302.14,
          "end": 307.08,
          "en": "If we now saved it and we do enter some values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.61,
          "end": 312.6,
          "en": "like a first request?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 314.38,
          "en": "And click add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 314.38,
          "end": 317.64,
          "en": "Nothing changes here, here we still see our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 317.64,
          "end": 320.37,
          "en": "because it still was stored in context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 320.37,
          "end": 324.4,
          "en": "But if we go to this backend, we now see this expenses note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.4,
          "end": 329.15,
          "en": "And in there we got this a item with this cryptic text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 329.15,
          "end": 332.61,
          "en": "that is this automatically generated unique ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.61,
          "end": 336.3,
          "en": "I mentioned before, and if we expand this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 336.3,
          "end": 338.82,
          "en": "we see the data we submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.82,
          "end": 340.55,
          "en": "And that of course is awesome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.55,
          "end": 344.063,
          "en": "because that proves that sending our data worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 345.15,
          "end": 347.14,
          "en": "Now that's a first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 347.14,
          "end": 349.49,
          "en": "We still got more work to do on the front end though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 349.49,
          "end": 351.21,
          "en": "We might want to add some feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 351.21,
          "end": 353.53,
          "en": "whilst the request is on its way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.53,
          "end": 357.15999999999997,
          "en": "We also might want to handle errors that could occur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 357.15999999999997,
          "end": 360.92,
          "en": "And we also might want to utilize this unique ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 360.92,
          "end": 363.45,
          "en": "that is generated on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 363.45,
          "end": 366.68,
          "en": "because at the moment I still also generate my own ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 366.68,
          "end": 368.21,
          "en": "And that for example means that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 368.21,
          "end": 371.2,
          "en": "if we would want to add it or delete this item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 371.2,
          "end": 374.9,
          "en": "we would have different ideas on the front end and backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 374.9,
          "end": 377.52,
          "en": "which could also lead to problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 377.52,
          "end": 380.27,
          "en": "So these are more things we can tackle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.27,
          "end": 382.41,
          "en": "but before we do any of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 382.41,
          "end": 385.57,
          "en": "let's make sure we actually utilize the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 385.57,
          "end": 388.38,
          "en": "to fetch our expenses from there as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 388.38,
          "end": 390.66,
          "en": "And that is the actual next thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.66,
          "end": 392.573,
          "en": "we will do in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
